---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="HaystaqDNA Models | Arkansas Campaign Data Cooperative" description="L2 HaystaqDNA preference models: 160+ issue, behavior, candidate, and turnout scores (0–100) for Arkansas campaign targeting.">
<section class="page-hero">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/data/">L2 Data</a> / Models</p>
        <p class="brand-lockup">L2 · HaystaqDNA</p>
        <h1 transition:name="page-title">160+ preference models. Scores from 0 to 100.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">The L2 HaystaqDNA models identify voters by likely feelings toward issues and candidates—and by behaviors that matter to campaign contact strategy. Available in L2 DataMapping and across digital platforms and integrations.</p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/assets/L2-Haystaq-Model-List.pdf">Download model list (PDF)</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://l2-data.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">L2 Data</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/data/">Full data architecture</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="exec-panel">
          <h3>How campaigns use the models</h3>
          <p>Each model is presented as a score from <strong>0–100</strong>, with flags to identify those most likely to support, oppose, or behave in a defined way. That lets serious campaigns move beyond party registration alone—into issue intensity, channel responsiveness, and turnout propensity.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="taxonomy-grid">
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Behavior</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Activism, charity, church attendance</li>
              <li>Email / SMS / live-call responsiveness</li>
              <li>Political donations, ticket splitters</li>
              <li>Ballot drop-off, community connection</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Economy</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Affordability, housing, inflation fault</li>
              <li>Unions, capitalism, income inequality</li>
              <li>Gig work, tax cuts, infrastructure</li>
              <li>Crypto, economic anxiety</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Healthcare &amp; education</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Abortion, ACA, Medicaid expansion</li>
              <li>Medicare for All, vaccines</li>
              <li>School choice, charter schools, funding</li>
              <li>Teachers union, CRT books</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Ideology &amp; partisanship</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Fiscal / social / general ideology</li>
              <li>Democrat type, Republican type</li>
              <li>Primary election ideology</li>
              <li>Third-party partisanship</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Environment &amp; government</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Climate, Green New Deal, gas tax</li>
              <li>Gun control, marijuana, death penalty</li>
              <li>Regulations, public transit</li>
              <li>Casino / online gambling</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Media &amp; consumer</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Podcast, social, TV news lean</li>
              <li>EV / solar / home buyer</li>
              <li>Rideshare, vaping, TV viewer</li>
              <li>Consumer value scores</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Military, borders &amp; foreign policy</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Defense spending, China policy</li>
              <li>Immigration &amp; border views</li>
              <li>Israel policy models</li>
              <li>Military family relationship</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Turnout</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Likely early / midterm / presidential</li>
              <li>Vote-by-mail propensity</li>
              <li>Combined turnout × mode models</li>
              <li>Unlikely presidential × likely VBM</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Candidates &amp; officials</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>National figure favorability models</li>
              <li>Female / minority candidate preference</li>
              <li>Age-limit and leadership models</li>
              <li>Horse-race support scores</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>

        <p class="lead">Also covered: political activism &amp; strife models, Trump-specific batteries, voting &amp; courts (RCV, redistricting, felon voting), and role-of-government issues.</p>
        <p>Source document: <a href="/assets/L2-Haystaq-Model-List.pdf">L2 Haystaq Model List (PDF)</a>. Learn more from L2 at <a href="mailto:info@L2-data.com">info@L2-data.com</a> or <a href="https://l2-data.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">l2-data.com</a>.</p>
        <div class="source-links">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/cooperative/">Fund cooperative access</a>
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/data/">Field dictionary overview</a>
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/join/?intent=demo">Schedule a briefing</a>
        </div>
        <p class="attr-note">HaystaqDNA model names and taxonomy © <a href="https://l2-data.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">L2, Inc.</a> / HaystaqDNA. Summarized here for Arkansas cooperative participants.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

</BaseLayout>
